\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Binary heads: test log loss (lower is better) and AUC for the marginal predictor, the tree baseline on summary features, and the surrogate.}}{9}{table.1}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Prong multiplicity head ($N \in \{0,\dots ,8\}$) among reconstructed events.}}{9}{table.2}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Event-by-event confusion between MasterAnaDev's prong count (rows, with the number of test events) and one surrogate draw (columns), row-normalised.}}{9}{table.3}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Event-level generated variables on reconstructed test events, in the model's robustly standardised space; one surrogate sample per event with the flags, multiplicity and vertex class also sampled.}}{11}{table.4}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Reconstruction outcome by true hadron species on single-hadron, single-prong events: MasterAnaDev / surrogate row fractions, and the proton-vs-pion AUC of the proton score among prongs with a proton fit.}}{14}{table.5}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Prong-level marginals: category fractions over all prongs, and median [16\%, 84\%] with $W_1$ for the continuous fields of prongs that have the corresponding fit.}}{16}{table.6}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Closure classifiers on the event-level variables: overall, by block, by single variable, and with the truth features added.}}{18}{table.7}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Closure AUC (0.5 is indistinguishable) with the evaluation's classifier recipe, on the nine generated variables and on the non-calorimetry subset that leaves out the non-vertex and isolated-blob energies, for the full test split and for the held-out 2p2h events, models A and B. ``+ truth'' adds the truth summary features, the flags and the multiplicity to the classifier. Values below 0.5 are fluctuations of an indistinguishable pair; the resolution of the test is about 0.005 on the full split and 0.01 on the 2p2h sample.}}{18}{table.8}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Closure of the prong set and the vertex plane.}}{19}{table.9}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Holdout summary. Columns: model A (trained with 2p2h) and model B (2p2h blind) on the 2p2h test events; B on the non-2p2h control; A on the full test split. The PID AUC on 2p2h is not meaningful (three pion-led events) and is listed only for completeness.}}{21}{table.10}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Per interaction type: share of CC $\nu _\mu $ events, classifier AUC against all other processes on the model inputs, fraction of the process located where the other processes' density is below 0.1 and below 0.01 of its own, and the median density ratio rest/process over the process's events.}}{23}{table.11}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Input-definition variants on the full test split: 50\,MeV without neutrons (ke50), 10\,MeV without neutrons (ke10), 10\,MeV with neutron tokens (ke10n).}}{24}{table.12}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces The same variants on the 2p2h test events.}}{24}{table.13}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces Previous model (exact zeros dequantised) against the present zero-flag model, both at 10\,MeV with neutrons. Closure AUC as marginal / truth-conditional; marginal pull RMS over the bins of Table~\ref {tab:bayes-bins}, model A, test control / held-out 2p2h, epistemic term only, for all observables and for the non-calorimetry set (without the two non-vertex calorimetric quantities); training time for both stages on one RTX~3090.}}{25}{table.14}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Pull RMS of the marginal bin fractions before and after adding the model-error floor derived on the training-split control.}}{30}{table.15}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces Bins of the calibration pulls. Logarithmic edges are listed in full; the integer variables use one bin per value. ``Populated'' counts the bins with at least 30 events on the control and on the held-out 2p2h sample.}}{32}{table.16}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {17}{\ignorespaces Composition of the all-events population (true vertex in the training volume) and of its test split. ``other'' is the handful of events without a CC or NC label.}}{40}{table.17}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {18}{\ignorespaces CC $\nu _\mu $ model A on its CC $\nu _\mu $ test split, and all-events model A on the CC $\nu _\mu $, NC, other (CC $\bar \nu _\mu $, $\nu _e$, $\bar \nu _e$) and full test splits: event counts, log losses of the binary and multiplicity heads, closure AUCs (overall and per block, truth-conditional) and $W_1$ in model space. The prong row gives the AUC on the prong summaries alone and with the truth features.}}{41}{table.18}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {19}{\ignorespaces Closure AUC with the recipe of Table~\ref {tab:closure-ci} on all nine variables and on the non-calorimetry set, for the CC $\nu _\mu $ models (upper rows, from Table~\ref {tab:closure-ci}) and the all-events models by test subset. Each value is one evaluation; the run-to-run variation is about 0.005 on the large samples and 0.01 to 0.02 on the 2p2h, NC and other CC samples.}}{41}{table.19}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {20}{\ignorespaces 2p2h holdout for the CC $\nu _\mu $ pair (Section~\ref {sec:holdout}) and the all-events pair: log losses and closure on the held-out 2p2h test events, B on its non-2p2h CC $\nu _\mu $ control, and the bootstrap evaluation of open dataset against B and against A (68\% intervals).}}{42}{table.20}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {21}{\ignorespaces Posterior-draw calibration of model A: pull RMS over the bins (number of bins, fraction within $|\mathrm {pull}|<2$) on the held-out 2p2h events and on a 300,000-event non-2p2h control, and the AUC with which the per-event epistemic quantities separate 2p2h from the control. The CC $\nu _\mu $ control is the like-for-like comparison; the all-events control is shown for completeness.}}{43}{table.21}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {22}{\ignorespaces Composition by flavour and current of the open dataset in the full training volume and of the inclusive NuWro and GiBUU samples (weighted shares), and the number of events; the generator samples are at 23.8\%{} of the open dataset's exposure.}}{44}{table.22}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {23}{\ignorespaces Inclusive samples through the all-events model A, events with the reconstructed vertex in the fiducial volume: number per event with the true vertex in it and per event of the sample, fraction with the true vertex outside (with its statistical error), split by region and, for those outside, by nucleus, and the fraction of reconstructed-fiducial events whose reconstructed vertex $z$ is more than 100\,mm from the true one.}}{45}{table.23}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {24}{\ignorespaces AUC of the per-event epistemic quantities of the surrogate for reconstructed-fiducial events: true vertex outside against inside the fiducial volume (surrogate on GENIE), and generator against GENIE among the events from outside.}}{47}{table.24}%
